  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To file a roof insurance claim in Utah, safely document all storm damage, hire a licensed local roofer for an independent inspection, and contact your insurance provider with your policy number and evidence. Make sure your contractor holds an active S280 General Roofing license through Utah DOPL.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Step-by-Step Claim Process"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Document damage: Take wide and close-up photos of bruised or creased shingles, dented gutters, damaged window wraps, and interior leaks. Save local weather reports or hail alerts.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              2,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Get a pre-inspection: Hire a local roofing contractor to perform a detailed inspection and itemize the damage before calling your insurer.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Verify licensing: Confirm your contractor has an S280 license via the Utah Division of Occupational and Professional Licensing (DOPL) .",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Utah Division of Occupational and Professional Licensing (DOPL)",
                "link": "https://www.dopl.utah.gov"
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "File the claim: Call your insurance company to report the date and cause of the damage, and ask if they will meet your contractor on-site during the adjuster's inspection.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Review the adjuster's report: Compare the carrier\u2019s line-item estimate against your contractor's report to check for missed collateral damage or local code requirements.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Important Utah Rules to Know"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Deductibles: Under Utah law, roofing contractors cannot legally pay, waive, or rebate your insurance deductible.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "The \"25% Rule\" Myth: Utah does not have a state-mandated 25% roof replacement rule; approvals depend on your specific policy language, local building codes, and whether discontinued shingles prevent a proper repair.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3,
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Supplements: If the insurance estimate leaves out required items, your contractor can submit a formal supplement letter with photos and measurements.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              7
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What type of storm caused the damage (hail, high wind, heavy snow)?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Has an adjuster already inspected your roof?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you prepare for the next step."
      }
    ],
